            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0596" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6367: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-06T16:00:00-04:00">May 6, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 267, May 5, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Please report date of Lamont’s memorandum and the date on which it was
                        given to the Embassy. Does the phrase in the memorandum “Thursday morning
                        next” mean May 6 or May 13?</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>You may inform Lamont that, favoring the principle of cooperation, the
                        Department feels that exploration of possibilities of its practical
                        application along the lines and under the circumstances outlined in Lamont’s
                        memorandum may serve a useful purpose.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
